Apache licenses (and files dual-licensed GPL-2.0 OR MIT, used under their
permissive option) as well as public documents. Each spec names every source
tree it cites in a resources.repos entry, with the commit and the SPDX license
of the cited files, and anchors each fact read from it to lines of that tree.

Facts drawn from BSD-, ISC- and MIT-licensed sources carry their source's
attribution. Where a spec reproduces material from such a source (a register
or symbol name, a constant, a short excerpt), the spec keeps that source's
copyright notice and license terms with it, in the spec's notices field, and
the spec and source are listed below. The reproduced
material stays under its source's license.

